{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>Between the unclean and between the clean.</b> In domesticated animal, in water swarming creature, and in fowl. After he explained to you these, he explained to you the law of the wild animal, and afterward the law of the woman who gives birth, and leprosy in man, in garment, etc. — for in all of them impurity applies." "<b>And between the wild animal that may be eaten.</b> Rashi: between one in which signs of terefah and of kosher developed, such as if he slaughtered the trachea and the lung was punctured before the slaughter of the esophagus — that is a sign of terefah [that the lung was punctured] and of kosher, because the life of the lung depends on the trachea. Between one in which signs of terefah and of disqualified developed, such as if the lung was punctured before he slaughtered the trachea; and so it is in tractate Ḥullin." "<b>And between the wild animal that you shall not eat.</b> It comes to give a warning for the wild animal. The order of the section of Shemini is well-established."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The word פרש״י at the head signals Rashi as the source being cited; rendered as 'Rashi:' to mark the transition from lemma to cited comment.", 2 "The final phrase שלימא סדרא דפרשת שמיני is a talmudic-style affirmation that the sequence/order of the parashah is now complete and well-arranged."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:36.677844837Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}